  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 consistently outperforms pca_n2000 across all tested settings (+0.04 to +0.07 acc), and the best configuration so far is config_042 (scvi_n200 + vit_l + avgpool + concat, 0.715 acc). However, scgpt has never been tested, leaving a major uncertainty about the RNA encoder landscape. Question: config_040 (scgpt + vit_l + avgpool + concat) is a clean A/B comparison against config_042, isolating the RNA encoder effect while holding image encoder, aggregation, and fusion at their best-known values. Why best next experiment: it tests the single most important unexplored design dimension (RNA encoder type) under the strongest known configuration. If scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it opens a new promising direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as the optimal RNA representation and redirects budget toward other axes (e.g., singleprofile, transformer aggregation). This is more informative than re-testing transformer aggregation (already shown to hurt in config_013 vs config_036) or image_only baselines (multimodal advantage is already well-established at +0.056 to +0.065 over rna_only)."
